Description: fate: check that AC-3 sync headers do not consume metadata
 Feed AC-3, dual-mono AC-3, independent E-AC-3 and dependent E-AC-3
 prefixes followed by two different metadata tails. Compare the parsed
 fields and bit counts against fixed references derived from the syntax.
 .
 Master consumes metadata in every case and rejects the dependent header
 with an all-ones tail. The bounded header reader returns identical basic
 fields for both tails. All input buffers have zeroed bitreader padding.
 No external sample or probabilistic repetition is needed.
 .
 Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
 Assisted-by: Claude Opus via Claude Code
